def policy(rid,title,finding,role,mechanism,output,outcome,attribution,ns,phase,proof=None):
    fields={'Initiative':title,'Finding':finding,'Documented role':role,'Mechanism / objective':mechanism,'Adoption / output':output,'Outcome evidence':outcome,'Attribution assessment':attribution}
    add('Policy & Governance',rid,fields,ns,'Analysis',proof=proof or {'Finding':ns},phase=phase)
policy('PG01','Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana','Rural Development Minister at PMGSY launch; his March 2001 answer explains programme goals and state implementation.','Led responsible ministry, 2000–2002','All-weather connectivity for eligible unconnected rural habitations.','Launched 25 December 2000; thresholds and deadlines were programme targets.','Later studies find labour reallocation and schooling effects, with limited measured consumption/income gains in the studied horizon.','Programme effects cannot be assigned solely to the launch-period minister.',[14,19],2,{'Finding':[14],'Outcome evidence':[19]})
policy('PG02','PMGSY: evaluating the outcome','Academic evidence qualifies a simple roads-equal-prosperity account.','Launch-period minister; studies cover later implementation','Researchers compare villages around eligibility population thresholds.','Road access increased in eligible villages; analysis uses roads completed well after his tenure.','Study summary reports movement out of agriculture and education gains, but no substantial income, consumption or asset changes after about four years.','Local study estimates are neither a lifetime national score nor a personal ministerial effect.',[19],2)
policy('PG03','Smart Cities Mission','His 2016 letter shows active implementation through competitive selection, special-purpose vehicles and requests for stable local management.','Ministerial implementation and Centre–state coordination','City proposals compete; SPVs receive funds; continuity of key officials encouraged.','Letter reports first 20 selected from 97 proposals and further rounds.','Inspected evidence establishes administrative design; no complete city-wide welfare evaluation assembled.','Central design depended on state and municipal capacity; SPV–municipal ambiguity is a documented governance concern.',[17,18],4,{'Finding':[17],'Attribution assessment':[17,18]})
policy('PG04','AMRUT','Responsible minister during 2015 launch of the 500-city water and sewerage mission.','Led responsible ministry; collective government initiative','Central assistance and state/city plans for urban infrastructure.','Launched 25 June 2015; five-year central allocation Rs 50,000 crore.','2017–2018 annual report extends beyond his exit; approvals or targets must not be counted as completed household connections.','Finance and delivery shared across governments; report alone cannot isolate his impact.',[1,13],4)
policy('PG05','PMAY (Urban)','Held the housing portfolio during the launch of central urban housing assistance in June 2015.','Responsible minister; programme implementation','Assistance to eligible urban households through programme components and participating governments/lenders.','PMAY(U) launched 25 June 2015 with a 2015–2022 mission horizon.','No tenure-bounded independent housing-completion evaluation assembled here.','Sanctioned units, completed units and occupied adequate housing are different outcomes.',[1,13],4)
policy('PG06','HRIDAY','Heritage-city infrastructure programme began during his urban tenure.','Responsible minister; associated executive leadership','Combine urban planning, economic activity and heritage conservation.','Launched 21 January 2015; 12 cities; Rs 500 crore programme outlay.','Annual report gives later project approvals; these do not establish conservation or livelihood outcomes.','Programme-level association is established; personal authorship and lasting local effects are not.',[1,13],4)
policy('PG07','RERA: legislative sponsorship','Moved the Real Estate Bill in Lok Sabha in March 2016 and steered its passage as responsible minister.','Sponsored and negotiated legislation','Project registration, disclosure and regulatory accountability for real-estate development.','Rajya Sabha passed 10 March; Lok Sabha 15 March; assent 25 March 2016.','Enactment established a regulatory framework; compliance and remedy effectiveness need state-level evaluation.','The bill’s 2013 origin and earlier policy work preclude sole-origin credit.',[15,16],4,{'Finding':[15],'Adoption / output':[16],'Attribution assessment':[15,16]})
policy('PG08','RERA: implementation','The remaining provisions took effect on 1 May 2017 during his housing tenure.','Implemented national framework','Registration, 70 percent separate project account and five-year defect obligations.','All 92 sections effective; states/UTs responsible for authorities and rules.','Press release is implementation guidance, not evidence that every buyer obtained relief.','Distinguish a national enabling statute from later regulatory performance.',[16,1],4)
policy('PG09','Swachh Survekshan and citizen tools','Launched the 2017 survey covering 500 cities and digital/telephone participation tools on 6 August 2016.','Launched administrative monitoring and public communication','Rankings combine local reports, citizen feedback and independent observation; app and helpline 1969 receive requests.','Survey scheduled for January 2017; Asli Tarakki campaign promoted toilet use.','Launch does not prove universal sanitation access or independently validated behaviour change.','National campaign, local service provision and personal ministerial promotion are separate contributions.',[36],4)
policy('PG10','Urban transport','Annual report records his inauguration of the Thirumangalam–Nehru Park Chennai Metro stretch in May 2017.','Responsible minister and inauguration participant','Metro construction and opening through project institutions.','Passenger services inaugurated 14 May 2017.','An opening is a concrete output; costs, ridership, distribution and prior planning require separate evaluation.','Do not assign a multi-year project solely to the minister who opened a segment.',[13],4)
policy('PG11','Andhra Pradesh assistance','Promised ten years of special status in 2014, then defended financial assistance in its place in September 2016.','Campaign advocate, later Union government defender','Proposed fiscal support for residual Andhra after state division.','2016 package was announced without granting special category status.','His claim that the package was superior is not an independently verified benefit comparison.','Demonstrates change in the offered policy instrument; collective Cabinet and fiscal decisions constrain individual attribution.',[38,39],4)
policy('PG12','Parliamentary committee work','Chaired Petitions and Home Affairs committees and an Enemy Property subcommittee before returning to Cabinet.','Oversight leadership','Committee examination rather than executive command.','Official profile records appointments, including Home Affairs August 2009–May 2014.','Report-specific recommendations, government uptake and effects have not been reconstructed.','A chairmanship establishes responsibility and opportunity, not automatic authorship of every recommendation.',[3],3)
policy('PG13','Multilingual Rajya Sabha','Interpretation expanded to all 22 scheduled languages during his chairmanship.','Institutional leadership with Secretariat implementation','Reduce language barriers in debate.','Expansion recorded from 18 July 2018.','Access mechanism documented; measured changes in participation by language not established.','Secretariat and interpreters share implementation credit.',[20],5)
policy('PG14','Committee monitoring and productivity','Secretariat retrospective credits monitoring and reports improved productivity in later sessions.','Chairman’s institutional supervision','Review attendance, meeting duration and use of House time.','For 13 full sessions through April 2022, productivity 68.35%; first five 42.77%, next eight 82.34%.','Time-use statistic does not establish deliberative quality or neutrality; controversy record must also be considered.','Party behaviour, government scheduling and pandemic conditions influence results; no isolated chairman effect.',[20,29,30,31],5,{'Finding':[20],'Adoption / output':[20],'Attribution assessment':[20,29,30,31]})
policy('PG15','Women’s political empowerment','Publicly advocated reservation in legislatures, equal property opportunities and action against son preference.','Advocacy as Vice-President','Speech urged political and social reforms, girls’ education and opposition to dowry.','Speech recorded 23 August 2020.','No causal evidence that this intervention itself changed enactment or women’s political representation.','Expressed support is distinct from party nominations, legislation and implementation.',[32,12],5,{'Finding':[32],'Attribution assessment':[12,32]})
policy('PG16','International representation','Held a UN-Habitat Governing Council presidency and later represented India at ASEM and NAM meetings.','Council presiding officer; vice-presidential representative','Multilateral representation in different institutional capacities.','Council election May 2017; official profile records ASEM 2018 and NAM 2019 representation.','No independently established personal diplomatic breakthrough claimed.','Representation is not equivalent to control of foreign policy or executive leadership of UN-Habitat.',[1,35],5)
policy('PG17','Voluntary social service','Official award citation praises Swarna Bharat Trust’s training and social work associated with Naidu.','Associated founder/public advocate as described by official sources','Training and community-service activities involving women and youth.','Government commendation in 2024.','No independently audited beneficiary or income effect established; separate trust-concession allegations appear in Controversies.','Ceremonial praise is attributed and does not substitute for audited programme effectiveness.',[34,23,40],6,{'Finding':[34]})

IDEAS=[
('Movement apprenticeship','Student unions, regional agitation, the JP movement and Emergency resistance supplied overlapping routes into politics.','Movement and organisational experience','These channels must not be collapsed into an uninterrupted national office.',[1,3,4],1),
('RSS and BJP affiliation','IANS describes a lifelong RSS/BJP ideological background and movement into national party leadership.','Reported biographical interpretation','Exact childhood joining dates and every ABVP title were not independently established.',[41],2),
('Cultural nationalism and coalition tensions','Contemporary reporting records criticism of his proposal to reproduce the Gujarat electoral experience; CPM pressed TDP to reconsider its NDA support.','2002 political controversy','Original full speech was not recovered; report establishes contemporary criticism, not personal responsibility for communal violence.',[43],2),
('Cross-party relationships','His participation in the NTR restoration campaign and reported friendships outside BJP supported a reputation as a communicator across party lines.','Organisational and alliance practice','Relationship evidence does not prove agreement on ideology or impartiality in later rulings.',[4,41],2),
('Organisation beyond direct elections','State and national party appointments and Rajya Sabha entry provided a route to national influence after repeated constituency defeats.','Analytical synthesis','Institutional pathway is documented; private motives and a single causal explanation are not.',[1,7,9,10,41],2),
('Communication','Profiles emphasise alliteration, acronyms, quick responses and public-speaking skill.','Journalistic assessment','Rhetorical fluency is not a measured policy or electoral effect.',[4,41],4),
('Centre–state implementation','The Smart Cities letter couples central competitive selection and funding conditions with requests to a state chief minister.','Primary ministerial correspondence','Federal coordination and central conditions coexist; neither pure decentralisation nor personal control captures the mechanism.',[17],4),
('Economic adaptation','In 2018 he recalled earlier opposition to automation and advocated adapting to technology while preserving cultural identity.','Attributed retrospective speech','Recollection establishes his stated account of change, not a reconstructed history of student economic platforms.',[42],5),
('Pluralism and national identity','At the ABVP convention he presented secularism as embedded in Indian culture, urged non-discrimination and advocated cultural content in education.','Attributed position','His confidence that secularism was safe is a political assessment, not an independent measurement of minority security.',[42],5),
('Debate, discipline and the chair','Promoted constructive debate and institutional order; opposition disputes show that the application of discipline remained contested.','Speeches plus procedural record','Stated aspiration and contested practice must be assessed together.',[3,20,29,30,31,44],5),
('Women’s political participation','Advocated legislative reservation, while earlier scholarly criticism questioned his explanation for women’s limited party candidacies.','Speech and academic critique','Different periods and different institutional powers; no simple claim of either consistency or hypocrisy follows.',[12,32],5),
('Language and access','Expansion of interpretation in Rajya Sabha provided an institutional expression of linguistic inclusion.','Recorded institutional action','No inference that all languages received identical use or resources.',[20],5),
('Civic duties after office','Public address in October 2026 linked citizens’ duties, skills and constructive politics with the 2047 development aspiration.','Attributed speech','Continued advocacy as a former Vice-President, not an executive programme under his authority.',[33],6),
('Publications and self-presentation','Official profile lists selected speeches and annual chronicles including Moving on…Moving forward and Listening, Learning and Leading.','Publication listing','Titles were located; books were not read in full and are not counted as independent evaluations.',[1],5)]
for i,(topic,finding,etype,limit,ns,phase) in enumerate(IDEAS,1):
    add('Ideas & Political Method',f'IM{i:02d}',{'Topic':topic,'Finding':finding,'Evidence type':etype,'Interpretive limit':limit},ns,'Analysis' if i in [1,4,5,7,10,11,12] else 'Attributed position',phase=phase)

def controversy(rid,matter,period,finding,criticism,response,forum,disposition,ns,phase,proof=None,independent=False,note=''):
    add('Controversies',rid,{'Matter':matter,'Period / latest inspected status':period,'Finding':finding,'Allegation / criticism':criticism,'Subject / government response':response,'Authority / forum':forum,'Procedural status / disposition':disposition},ns,'Attributed position',proof=proof or {'Finding':ns},phase=phase,priority='High',independent=independent,note=note)
controversy('CO01','2004 defeat and departure from BJP presidency','2004','National election defeat preceded his departure; Advani’s account gives personal/family reasons for the request to step down.','Party leadership faced the consequences of losing national power.','Stated reason was personal and family considerations; Advani publicly praised his service.','BJP leadership / National Council','Political resignation and succession, not an adjudicated finding of sole responsibility.',[22,1],2,note='Do not substitute inferred punishment or hidden factional motives for the reported explanation.')
controversy('CO02','Gujarat electoral rhetoric and coalition criticism','December 2002','CPM criticised his reported advocacy of repeating the Gujarat electoral experience and pressed Chandrababu Naidu over NDA support.','B. V. Raghavulu challenged the consistency of the BJP position with the coalition’s common agenda.','Full original presidential speech not retrieved; detailed personal rebuttal not established in inspected report.','Political debate','Contemporary criticism documented; no legal finding about Naidu is asserted.',[43],2,note='Two Naidus must be distinguished. Primary speech and broader contextual scholarship remain a research gap.')
controversy('CO03','Kushabhau Thakre Memorial Trust land allotment','Supreme Court judgment, 6 April 2011','Supreme Court quashed the 20-acre Bhopal allotment to a trust whose first president was Naidu.','Court criticised allocation of public land without transparent opportunity for competing institutions.','The judgment records the respondent trust’s defence; the inspected record does not establish a separate personal statement by Naidu.','Supreme Court, Civil Appeal 2965/2011','Allotment and related notifications quashed; repossession and refund directed. This is not a personal criminal conviction.',[24],3,proof={'Finding':[24],'Procedural status / disposition':[24]},note='Primary judicial disposition controls. Initial request and final allotment sizes must not be confused.')
controversy('CO04','Swarna Bharat Trust development-charge concession','July 2017 allegations and responses','Congress questioned a concession involving the trust associated with his daughter; government/BJP responses said similar relief applied to other nonprofits.','Congress alleged preferential treatment; subsequent IANS report also relayed an alleged FCRA notice.','Naidu denied wrongdoing and political targeting was alleged; Telangana minister K. T. Rama Rao cited concessions for other nonprofits.','Political allegations; relevant administrative records not independently obtained','Allegations and denials documented. No merits finding or final FCRA disposition established in this research.',[23,40],4,independent=True,note='Trust administration, government concessions and criminal wrongdoing are separate questions. Underlying FCRA notice not inspected.')
controversy('CO05','Police vehicle procurement and son’s dealership','July 2017','Congress challenged police vehicle procurement involving his son’s dealership; Telangana defended use of centrally fixed procurement rates.','Alleged absence of tender and family-linked benefit.','Government cited DGS&D rates; BJP’s K. Laxman denied Naidu’s involvement in his son’s business.','Political and administrative dispute','No final procurement audit or judicial merits finding recovered. Reported vehicle counts differ and are not combined into one verified number.',[23,40],4,independent=True)
controversy('CO06','Earlier Nellore land allegations','Revived July 2017','Congress revived allegations about land acquired earlier; Naidu denied wrongdoing and said courts had dismissed earlier cases.','Political accusation concerning land intended for disadvantaged people.','Dismissal is recorded as Naidu’s response, not as an independently checked court disposition.','Political exchange; original land/court files not retrieved','Unresolved in this evidence set; neither guilt nor exoneration independently established.',[23],4,note='Do not merge this with the separate Supreme Court Bhopal trust judgment.')
controversy('CO07','NDTV India one-day prohibition','November 2016','As I&B Minister, Naidu defended a one-day prohibition over Pathankot reporting; the ministry subsequently put it on hold for review.','Broadcaster disputed security rationale and said other channels aired similar material; press-freedom criticism followed.','Naidu invoked national security and programme-code rules and called criticism politically motivated.','Information and Broadcasting Ministry; broadcaster’s court challenge','Administrative order held pending review on 7 November. Inspected record does not establish a final judicial merits judgment.',[25,26],4,independent=True,note='Record the order, defence and hold separately; a proposed one-day ban is not evidence it was ultimately served.')
controversy('CO08','Andhra special-status promise and package','April 2014–September 2016','His ten-year special-status promise was followed by a defence of a package that stopped short of that status.','Opposition criticised failure to deliver promised special category status.','Naidu argued the package was more beneficial and cited fiscal arrangements; he also criticised Congress’s reorganisation legislation.','Campaign and Union-government policy','Policy-instrument change established. Claimed financial superiority and impossibility of status are attributed assertions.',[38,39],4,note='Two separately dated PTI reports establish different statements, not independent audits of fiscal effects.')
controversy('CO09','Refusal to admit CJI removal notice','23 April–8 May 2018','Naidu refused admission of a motion seeking Chief Justice Dipak Misra’s removal; the court challenge was later withdrawn.','Congress MPs disputed the chairman’s threshold decision; counsel also contested the constitution of the Supreme Court bench hearing the challenge.','His order characterised the charges as conjectural and insufficient for admission.','Rajya Sabha Chairman; Supreme Court petition','Notice not admitted; petition dismissed as withdrawn. Neither event was a parliamentary trial or Supreme Court endorsement on the merits.',[27,28],5,proof={'Finding':[27,28],'Subject / government response':[27],'Procedural status / disposition':[27,28]},note='Admissibility and proved wrongdoing are different legal stages.')
controversy('CO10','Farm-bill proceedings and eight MPs’ suspension','20–21 September 2020','Harivansh chaired disputed farm-bill voice votes; the following day Naidu presided as the House suspended eight MPs and rejected notice against the Deputy Chairman.','Opposition demanded divisions; Indian Express video review challenged claims that requests were not made from seats.','Naidu condemned disorder and cited notice requirements; secretariat sources defended Harivansh amid disruption.','Rajya Sabha','House adopted suspension for remainder of session on ministerial motion. Naidu was not presiding over the previous day’s farm-bill passage.',[29,30],5,proof={'Finding':[29,30],'Allegation / criticism':[30],'Procedural status / disposition':[29]},note='Same news organisation but distinct reporting and video reconstruction; no false claim of two institutionally independent publications.')
controversy('CO11','Twelve MPs’ suspension across sessions','November–December 2021','Suspensions for conduct in the previous session prompted a procedural dispute; Naidu resisted revocation and later rejected a notice to terminate them.','Opposition questioned using previous-session conduct and the suspension procedure.','On 30 November he cited lack of remorse; December reporting attributed rejection of a notice to absence of the proposed motion text.','Rajya Sabha','House suspension and chairman’s procedural decisions; no judicial merits disposition established.',[31,44],5,independent=True)

LEGACY=[
('National organiser from Andhra','His career demonstrates a route from state movement politics to national party and constitutional leadership without a Lok Sabha victory among the six confirmed direct contests.','Workbook synthesis','Organisational assignments, indirect representation and ministerial expertise sustained influence.','Limited direct electoral success cautions against equating national office with a large personal constituency base.',[1,5,7,8,9,10,37,41],2),
('Rural infrastructure','PMGSY is an enduring programme associated with his rural ministry, but evidence warrants bounded credit.','Workbook synthesis using academic evaluation','Launch-period leadership and programme defence are documented.','Later implementation and measured effects extend far beyond his tenure; roads alone did not transform every studied economic outcome.',[14,19],2),
('Urban regulatory record','RERA provides a clearer legislative contribution than broad claims to have transformed Indian cities.','Workbook synthesis','His sponsorship and implementation roles are traceable.','Prior UPA-era bill development and state enforcement limit sole-credit narratives.',[15,16],4),
('Urban governance trade-offs','Smart Cities implementation shows active management alongside concerns over local democratic accountability.','CPR and workbook synthesis','Competitive proposals and stable-management requests supplied an implementation framework.','Taraporevala questions opaque SPV–municipality relationships and their implications for democratic processes.',[17,18],4),
('Parliamentary stewardship','Language access and administrative attention are documented achievements; neutrality and opposition rights remain contested dimensions.','Secretariat account compared with independent reporting','Multilingual access and reported later-session productivity.','CJI notice, farm-bill aftermath and suspension disputes prevent a single uncontested assessment.',[20,27,28,29,30,31,44],5),
('Gender and representation','Pro-reservation advocacy does not by itself settle his record as a party gatekeeper.','Amrita Basu and later speech record','2020 speech supported political empowerment and broader equality.','Basu criticises the scarcity-of-women explanation; women’s selection and outcomes require separate evidence.',[12,32],5),
('Communication and alliance relationships','Profiles portray an effective, witty communicator with cross-party friendships.','Contemporary journalists','Skill in organisation and public language helped bridge regional and national politics.','Friendships and wit are reputational assets, not a substitute for assessing decisions.',[4,41],4),
('Formal national recognition','Padma Vibhushan in 2024 is an official honour for his public-affairs career.','Government of India','Citation praises political and social-service contributions.','Ceremonial praise is interested evidence; chronology errors in that citation require independent office records.',[34,1],6),
('After constitutional office','October 2026 public advocacy shows continued participation in national civic debate.','Dated public reporting','Skills, duties and constructive parliamentary conduct remain themes.','Public speeches do not establish continuing executive authority or quantified policy influence.',[33],6)]
for i,(theme,finding,assessor,supporting,competing,ns,phase) in enumerate(LEGACY,1):
    add('Legacy & Assessments',f'LA{i:02d}',{'Theme':theme,'Finding':finding,'Assessor':assessor,'Supporting view':supporting,'Competing view / limit':competing},ns,'Analysis',phase=phase)

